<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17166" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-sănĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exan-</span></b> ), āre,
			v. a.
		sanies, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to free from matter</i> or <i>corruption</i>, <i>to cause to suppurate</i>,
				<i>to cleanse</i>, <i>dress</i> a
			wound, etc. (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnus (sal aridus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					5, 27</span></i>
			.—<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pressam bacam,</span>”
				<i>to press out the juice</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 47, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinapi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 57, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salsuram carnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 55, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">veterani, quamvis confossi, patienter et sine
					gemitu velut aliena corpora exsaniari patiuntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. ad Helv. 3, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amaritudinem et pallorem,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to extract</i>, <i>remove</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 55</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
